.TH PERVIUS 1 "2026-11-18" "Pervius" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pervius \- unofficial Linux client for FastVPN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pervius
.RB [ \-\-hidden ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pervius
starts the Pervius desktop application, a GTK 4/libadwaita client for an
existing FastVPN (OpenVPN) subscription. It validates the provider's public
server catalogue and imports the selected profile through NetworkManager and
its OpenVPN plugin. Passwords are supplied by a NetworkManager secret agent and
are never written into the profile.
.PP
Run it as your desktop user, never as root. NetworkManager performs the
privileged network operations. The optional kill switch is controlled through
.BR pervius\-killswitch (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start in the tray without showing the window (used by Start at login). If no
tray is available, the window is shown.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pervius/
Settings, favorites, cached catalogue, CA file and ownership manifest. No
passwords.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/com.solvetus.Pervius.desktop
Present only while Start at login is on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pervius\-killswitch (1),
.BR pervius\-inspect (1),
.BR pervius\-proof (1),
.BR nmcli (1)
